course: dictionary
lesson: 85
title: The word actress
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: An actress is a woman or girl who acts. She pretends to be a character in a play, a film or a TV show. Look at the clues in the sentence to understand the word. «Nan is glued to the telly: Prince Harry is marrying Meghan Markle, an American actress, at St George's Chapel in Windsor.» The words «glued to the telly» show Nan is watching TV, and the word between two commas, «an American actress», tells you what Meghan Markle does for work.
explain: Actress is a noun, and it ends in -ess because it is about a woman or girl. The same job for a man is an actor. Many women today prefer to be called actor, so you will see both words. Try the test: swap in «a famous actress» or «a child actress» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with the informal meaning. If someone is «a good actress», she is good at pretending feelings she does not really have. Nobody is saying she is a real actress on a stage, just that she fooled everyone.
fact: An actress is a woman or girl who acts in plays, films or TV shows.
fact: An actress pretends to be a character, which means she plays someone who is not herself.
fact: Many women today prefer to be called actor, the same word as for men.
fact: «Best actress» is the name of an award for the best woman in a film.
fact: Informally, «a good actress» means someone who is good at pretending feelings she does not really have.
exercise: «Meghan Markle, an American actress, married Prince Harry in 2018.» What is an actress? | A song sung at weddings | A place where films are made | A woman who sells tickets at the cinema | *A woman or girl who acts in plays, films or TV shows
exercise: Many women today prefer to be called what, the same word men use? | audience | director | *actor | singer
exercise: Ella says, «She is a good actress.» Her friend pretended to be happy when she was sad. What does Ella mean? | Her friend is a famous film star who won an award | Her friend is good at drawing faces | Her friend is always happy | *Her friend is good at pretending feelings she does not really have
test: Which phrase means a girl who acts in films when she is young? | stage door | *child actress | film critic | leading actress
test: Which word could replace actress in «an American actress» and still be used today by many women? | singer | writer | *actor | teacher
exam: Which sentence uses actress correctly? | The actress wrote the report for the school newspaper | The actress sang the national anthem at the match | *The actress pretended to be a queen in the film | The actress kicked the winning goal in the match
